{"id":"leetcode-1134","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Armstrong Number","summary":"Determine if an integer n is an Armstrong number by checking if the sum of its digits each raised to the power of the number of digits equals n.","statement":"Determine if an integer n is an Armstrong number by checking if the sum of its digits each raised to the power of the number of digits equals n.","constraints":["Raise each decimal digit to the total digit count.","Return whether their sum equals n."],"topics":["math"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"is_armstrong_number","parameters":[{"name":"n","annotation":"int","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"bool","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def is_armstrong_number(n: int) -> bool:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def is_armstrong_number(n):\n digits=str(n);return sum(int(char)**len(digits) for char in digits)==n\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def is_armstrong_number(n):\n digits=str(n);return sum(int(char)**2 for char in digits)==n\n","def is_armstrong_number(n):\n digits=str(n);return sum(int(char)**len(digits) for char in digits)!=n\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(digits)","target_space_complexity":"O(digits)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["The exponent is fixed by the number’s decimal width.","Convert to text to obtain all digits and their count.","Sum int(digit)**width and compare with n.","This is the Armstrong definition applied directly to every decimal digit."],"editorial":"This is the Armstrong definition applied directly to every decimal digit.","tests":[{"id":"lc-1134-1","arguments":[153],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"1^3+5^3+3^3 equals 153.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":